// GUARD for review fix #74 (7 Oct 2026; guard added after the review of
// 27 Oct 2026): `phi_ratio : critical_ratio` is the Flory-Huggins critical
// composition phi_A/phi_B = sqrt(N_B/N_A) of the delta_molecules pair
// (f''' = 0 for the binary blend). Namics uses the inverse sqrt(N_A/N_B),
// so this case DEVIATES from the oracle by design, and
// a Namics re-sync (or an A/B swap of delta_molecules) must turn it red.
// (A)100 restricted + (B)10 solvent, chi_AB 0.3, planar mirror box:
// start 1 nucleates an A slab (pinned 1..30), start 2 releases it, start 3
// pins the composition at layer 30 to the critical ratio. Expected and
// measured at creation (28 Oct 2026): kal phi_ratio = sqrt(10/100) =
// 0.316228, and in the start-3 profile phi_A - phi_B at layer 30 =
// (r-1)/(r+1) = -0.5194938533 (pro: -0.5194938539). With the inverted
// ratio (explicit phi_ratio : 3.16227766) the pinned difference flips to
// +0.519 and the .pro fails by orders of magnitude. theta_A 20, not 30: a
// fully filled pinned slab diverges on release. The phi_ratio column is NiN
// (with a warning) on the two starts without the constraint.
lat : NN : n_layers : 60
lat : NN : geometry : planar
lat : NN : lowerbound : mirror
lat : NN : upperbound : mirror

mon : A : freedom : pinned
mon : A : pinned_range : 1;30
mon : B : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_B : 0.3

mol : A : composition : (A)100
mol : A : freedom : restricted
mol : A : theta : 20
mol : B : composition : (B)10
mol : B : freedom : solvent

newton : n : tolerance : 1e-9

output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : A : theta
kal : sys : NN : phi_ratio
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential
output : pro : append : false
pro : mol : A : phi
pro : mol : B : phi
start
mon : A : freedom : free
start
sys : NN : constraint : delta
sys : NN : delta_molecules : A;B
sys : NN : delta_range : (30)
sys : NN : phi_ratio : critical_ratio
start
